export declare const keyboardBody = "\n    <div class=\"keeb-card\">\n        <h1>Keyboards</h1>\n        <p>\n            As a bored middle-schooler during the Covid lockdowns, I was scrolling through YouTube when I came across a video about custom keyboards. Since I had \n            nothing else to do I looked into it and found all kinds of sound tests with different words I'd never heard of before like thocky and clacky. I bought\n            a really simply custom keyboard called the Epomaker EP84 which was kind of my gateway into the hobby with which I learned to do all kinds of mods like\n            lubing switches and tuning stabilizers. I posted my first sound test on YouTube in 2022 which got a suprising number of views, prompting me to post more.\n            I experiemented with different kinds of videos and eventually had companies start reaching out to me to make reviews for them which was great since I \n            didn't have my own money and the custom keyboard hobby is not particularly cheap. Although I don't really post videos anymore since I'm a bit busy with\n            school and other activities, you can still find my old videos on my <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@SimulatorTech\" target=\"_blank\">YouTube Channel.</a> \n            The following is a small list of my favorite pieces from my collection.\n        </p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"keeb-card\">\n        <h2>Beloved Kohaku</h2>\n        <p>\n            When I first got into keyboards, I saw a lot of reviewers and keyboard influencers talk about the SingaKBD Kohaku and when I discovered how hard and\n            expensive it was to acquire, I decided it wasn't for me. That is, until my cousin, who purchased the GMK Beloved set, offered to let me buy his spot for\n            the Beloved Kohaku. Given it was a few years later and I had a little bit of money, I couldn't say no. Now that I have it, I can honestly say this keyboard\n            has incredible tolerances, build quality, and visuals, but it's popularity is entirely from FOMO and hype. That being said, it's one of my favorite keyboards\n            I own and probably the most expensive.\n        </p>\n        <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=s71XL5FgVmQ\" target=\"_blank\">Sound Demo</a>\n        <h3>Build Specs</h3>\n        <ul>\n            <li>Plate: Included Aluminum Plate</li>\n            <li>PCB: Included Solder PCB</li>\n            <li>Switches: Vintage Cherry MX Blacks\n                <ul>\n                    <li>Pulled from an 80's Wyse Terminal Board</li>\n                    <li>Broken in for 4 million actuations</li>\n                    <li>TX 0.15mm Films</li>\n                    <li>Spirit Extreme II 68g Springs oiled with 105g0</li>\n                    <li>Stem lightly lubed with 205g0</li>\n                </ul>\n            </li>\n            <li>Stabilizers: Cherry Clip-Ins\n                <ul>\n                    <li>Wires Lubed with Dielectric Grease</li>\n                    <li>Stems Holee Modded and Lubed with 205g0</li>\n                </ul>\n            </li>\n            <li>Keycaps: JTK Tripleshot Night Sakura</li>\n        </ul>\n\n        <div class=\"carousel-container\">\n            <div class=\"carousel-slide\">\n                <img src=\"/public/keyboard-images/kohaku/IMG_4212.JPG\" alt=\"keeb img 1\" class=\"active\">\n                <img src=\"/public/keyboard-images/kohaku/IMG_4213.JPG\" alt=\"keeb img 2\">\n                <img src=\"/public/keyboard-images/kohaku/IMG_4214.JPG\" alt=\"keeb img 3\">\n                <img src=\"/public/keyboard-images/kohaku/IMG_4215.JPG\" alt=\"keeb img 4\">\n                <img src=\"/public/keyboard-images/kohaku/IMG_4216.JPG\" alt=\"keeb img 5\">\n                <img src=\"/public/keyboard-images/kohaku/IMG_4217.JPG\" alt=\"keeb img 6\">\n            </div>\n            <button class=\"prev-btn\">&#10094;</button>\n            <button class=\"next-btn\">&#10095;</button>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n\n\n";
